<#part type=text/html>
<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><title>Monica Daily Growth Brief — 21 July 2026</title></head><body style="margin:0;background:#f3f6f8;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1f2937;line-height:1.45"><div style="max-width:850px;margin:0 auto;background:#fff;padding:28px"><div style="border-bottom:5px solid #0f766e;padding-bottom:16px"><div style="font-size:12px;color:#0f766e;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:1px">ALFRED TRAVEL</div><h1 style="margin:5px 0 0;font-size:27px;color:#102a43">Monica Daily Growth Brief</h1><div style="font-size:16px;color:#52606d">User Growth, Activation and Retention</div><div style="margin-top:10px;font-size:13px;color:#52606d">Report date: 21 July 2026 · Prepared at 08:00 AEST</div></div>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Today’s Growth Decision</h2><div style="background:#fff4e5;border-left:5px solid #d97706;padding:14px 16px"><strong>Do not materially scale acquisition. Maintain controlled acquisition while reliability, attribution and retention measurement are repaired.</strong><p style="margin:8px 0 0">The freshest complete Metabase window is 13–19 July 2026 UTC: 346 real itineraries, 306 ACTIVE and 54 hard failures. That is 88.4% ACTIVE output but a 15.6% hard-failure rate; the dominant alfred_plus path failed 54/94 times (57.4%). This fails the &lt;5% reliability gate. Firebase event-level refresh is unavailable today, so there is no current validated retention or event-funnel basis for scaling.</p></div>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Evidence Freshness</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Source</th><th>Evidence window / data through</th><th>Freshness</th><th>What it can support</th></tr><tr><td>Metabase live snapshot</td><td>Refreshed 21 Jul 2026 08:08 AEST; visible failed rows through 19 Jul 2026 UTC</td><td style="color:#166534"><strong>Current snapshot</strong></td><td>Confirms current activity and latest failed-row presence; not a complete funnel.</td></tr><tr><td>Metabase latest complete window</td><td>13–19 Jul 2026 UTC; data through 19 Jul</td><td style="color:#166534"><strong>2 days old; current complete window</strong></td><td>Real demand, ACTIVE output, failure rates and mode concentration.</td></tr><tr><td>Firebase / Jessica event analysis</td><td>Current refresh unavailable; Events explorer shell/iframe did not hydrate on 21 Jul. Last verified event window was historical and is not used for today’s current claims.</td><td style="color:#b91c1c"><strong>Unavailable</strong></td><td>No current event-level activation, retention, platform or push decisioning. DAU/old event data cannot substitute.</td></tr><tr><td>GA4</td><td>Last 7 days: 12–18 Jul 2026; data through 18 Jul</td><td style="color:#166534"><strong>3 days old; usable baseline</strong></td><td>Pre-launch website acquisition and engagement baseline only; Website V2 launched 20 Jul.</td></tr><tr><td>Website and SEO</td><td>Website V2 uploaded 20 Jul 2026; repo validated through 20 Jul commit; sitemap/robots and GA4 wiring present</td><td><strong>Launch observation period</strong></td><td>Publish status and conversion surfaces. First 24–72h is instrumentation/indexing observation, not impact proof.</td></tr><tr><td>Social / creative intelligence</td><td>Helen brief refreshed 21 Jul 2026 08:00 AEST; data through today</td><td style="color:#b45309"><strong>Current, access degraded</strong></td><td>Access limitation: Foreplay timed out, TikTok did not hydrate, Instagram login-gated; no new verified creative signal.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Growth Scorecard</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Area</th><th>Latest validated result</th><th>Assessment</th><th>Next gate</th></tr><tr><td>Real itinerary demand</td><td>346, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td>Demand is present, but not proof of broad acquisition quality.</td><td>Reconcile users, source and first itinerary.</td></tr><tr><td>ACTIVE output</td><td>306/346 = <strong>88.4%</strong>, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td>Above 85% gate overall.</td><td>Hold while mode-level failures remain high.</td></tr><tr><td>Overall hard-failure rate</td><td>54/346 = <strong>15.6%</strong>, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td style="color:#b91c1c"><strong>Reliability blocked.</strong></td><td>&lt;5% on a complete window.</td></tr><tr><td>Primary-mode hard-failure rate</td><td>alfred_plus: 54/94 = <strong>57.4%</strong>, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td style="color:#b91c1c">Critical path is failing.</td><td>&lt;5%, with failure reasons reconciled.</td></tr><tr><td>Cleanest-performing mode</td><td>Unknown/legacy mode: 306 ACTIVE, 0 hard failures from 346, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td>Strong result, but JSON mode coverage is incomplete.</td><td>Normalize mode taxonomy before comparing.</td></tr><tr><td>Day-1 retention</td><td>Current validated Firebase result unavailable on 21 Jul</td><td>Measurement blocked.</td><td>Hydrated event-level cohort result, overall/Android/iOS.</td></tr><tr><td>Android retention</td><td>Current validated Firebase result unavailable on 21 Jul</td><td>Measurement blocked.</td><td>Platform-specific D1 cohort.</td></tr><tr><td>iOS retention</td><td>Current validated Firebase result unavailable on 21 Jul</td><td>Measurement blocked.</td><td>Platform-specific D1 cohort.</td></tr><tr><td>Push performance</td><td>Current event/campaign refresh unavailable</td><td>Do not infer from DAU or old campaign cards.</td><td>FCM coverage, open and downstream return event.</td></tr><tr><td>Trustworthy bookings</td><td>0 booking-confirmation rows in 13–19 Jul UTC; table last recorded 10 Jul</td><td>No current booking evidence; recorded confirmation is not payment proof.</td><td>1:1 unique confirmation ID to journey.</td></tr><tr><td>Sample-data pollution</td><td>45 [SAMPLE] rows / 874 broader rows = <strong>5.1%</strong>, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td>Separate from production KPIs; lower than prior July baseline.</td><td>Keep real-only default and show sample share.</td></tr><tr><td>Organic acquisition</td><td>GA4 12–18 Jul: 42 active users from google/organic; 63 organic-search sessions</td><td>Pre-launch baseline; not Website V2 impact.</td><td>Post-launch, source-to-itinerary downstream tracking.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">What is Working</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Signal</th><th>Evidence</th><th>How Monica should use it</th></tr><tr><td>Real demand exists</td><td>346 real itineraries in 13–19 Jul UTC, excluding [SAMPLE] and internal/test accounts.</td><td>Protect demand with a reliable primary itinerary path rather than adding paid volume.</td></tr><tr><td>Overall output clears the broad gate</td><td>306 ACTIVE / 346 real = 88.4%, 13–19 Jul UTC.</td><td>Use as a recovery target, not permission to scale while alfred_plus is failing.</td></tr><tr><td>Non-alfred_plus path is cleaner</td><td>346 normalized-unknown-mode rows produced 306 ACTIVE and 0 hard failures, 13–19 Jul UTC.</td><td>Inspect the mode split and route more traffic only if taxonomy and cohort equivalence are validated.</td></tr><tr><td>Organic search is a meaningful pre-launch surface</td><td>GA4 12–18 Jul: 63 organic-search sessions and 42 google/organic active users.</td><td>Use Website V2 to capture intent, but wait for post-launch downstream conversion evidence.</td></tr><tr><td>Content surface is broad</td><td>GA4 12–18 Jul: homepage 267 views, About 66, features 40, itineraries 22 and blog 22.</td><td>Prioritize internal linking and one clear Plan a Trip CTA; do not claim conversion lift yet.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Largest Growth Leaks</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Priority</th><th>Leak</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Business impact</th></tr><tr><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>alfred_plus generation reliability</td><td>54 hard failures / 94 real = 57.4%, 13–19 Jul UTC.</td><td>Users cannot reach activation; paid traffic would amplify failure.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>Overall hard failures above scale gate</td><td>54 / 346 = 15.6%, versus required &lt;5%, 13–19 Jul UTC.</td><td>Planner trust and repeat use are at risk.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>Retention and event-funnel observability</td><td>Firebase current refresh unavailable; event explorer did not hydrate.</td><td>No trustworthy current activation, D1 retention or platform diagnosis.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>Booking attribution</td><td>0 booking-confirmation rows in 13–19 Jul UTC; last table row 10 Jul.</td><td>Monetization cannot be used as a scaling signal.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Cross-system acquisition reconciliation</td><td>GA4 shows 116 active users and 156 sessions for 12–18 Jul, while Metabase measures itineraries on a different grain/window.</td><td>Channel quality and payback cannot be assigned confidently.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>Creative intelligence access</td><td>Helen 21 Jul: Foreplay timeout, TikTok shell, Instagram login gate.</td><td>Creative decisions would rely on unverified examples.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Seven-Day Action Plan</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Priority</th><th>Action</th><th>Owner</th><th>Success measure</th><th>Scaling gate</th></tr><tr><td><strong>P0</strong></td><td>Triage alfred_plus failures by route, provider, timeout and response reason; add a safe fallback state.</td><td>Engineering</td><td>alfred_plus hard-failure rate &lt;5% over a fresh 7-day complete window; no unexplained FAILED-DISABLED burst.</td><td>Keep acquisition controlled until met.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P0</strong></td><td>Repair Firebase Events explorer hydration and publish a canonical event table.</td><td>Jessica / Analytics</td><td>Current event window with signup → first_open → generate → ACTIVE → view/save/share → return cohorts; overall, Android and iOS separated.</td><td>Measurement unblocked only after row-level event validation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P0</strong></td><td>Reconcile booking confirmation UUIDs to itinerary and user journey; deduplicate writes.</td><td>Data / Engineering</td><td>Every counted booking has one unique confirmation ID and journey mapping; duplicate rate reported.</td><td>No monetization scaling claim before reconciliation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P1</strong></td><td>Build daily acquisition-quality cut joining GA4 source/session, signup, first itinerary and downstream intent.</td><td>Growth Analytics</td><td>One comparable cohort table by source and platform with matched user grain.</td><td>Only scale channels whose downstream activation holds.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P1</strong></td><td>Improve first-week activation for users who generate but do not return; validate notification readiness.</td><td>Product / CRM</td><td>D1 retention and return session measured by Android/iOS; FCM coverage and notification downstream event visible.</td><td>Controlled messaging only until D1 is stable/improving.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P2</strong></td><td>Observe Website V2 launch and tighten homepage → Plan a Trip path/internal links.</td><td>Jessica / Web</td><td>Post-launch 7-day GA4 baseline with CTA click, webapp arrival and qualified itinerary generation.</td><td>No V2 lift claim before full post-launch window.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Recommended Growth Experiments</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Experiment</th><th>Proposition</th><th>Primary success metric</th><th>Secondary metrics</th></tr><tr><td>Reliable-path CTA test</td><td>Route qualified website visitors to the validated itinerary path, not the failing alfred_plus path.</td><td>Qualified itinerary generation → successful ACTIVE itinerary rate.</td><td>CTA click, webapp arrival, hard failures, time to ACTIVE.</td></tr><tr><td>First-plan return prompt</td><td>After a successful itinerary, show one practical next action: view, save or share.</td><td>Return session within 7 days.</td><td>Itinerary view, save/share, D1 retention by platform.</td></tr><tr><td>Intent-led landing page</td><td>Test family/multi-city logistics copy against generic AI-planning copy after V2 instrumentation is live.</td><td>Qualified itinerary generation per organic session.</td><td>CTA click, session engagement, ACTIVE output, booking intent.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Billy’s Decisions Today</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Decision required</th><th>Recommendation</th></tr><tr><td>Acquisition budget</td><td>Approve controlled acquisition only; no material paid scaling until overall hard failures are &lt;5%, alfred_plus is validated, and Firebase/booking attribution are trustworthy.</td></tr><tr><td>Engineering priority</td><td>Assign P0 ownership for alfred_plus reliability, Firebase hydration and booking-confirmation deduplication this week.</td></tr><tr><td>Website V2 measurement</td><td>Approve a 72-hour observation period followed by a 7-day post-launch baseline; do not use pre-launch GA4 as V2 lift evidence.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Overall Status</h2><p style="font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#b91c1c;border-top:3px solid #b91c1c;padding-top:12px">Growth status: Reliability blocked</p><p>Metabase demand and overall ACTIVE output are encouraging, but the 15.6% hard-failure rate and 57.4% alfred_plus failure rate fail the scaling gate. Current Firebase event-level measurement is unavailable, and booking attribution is not trustworthy enough to support a scale decision.</p><p style="font-size:11px;color:#667085;border-top:1px solid #d0d5dd;padding-top:10px">Evidence note: percentages independently recalculated from refreshed Metabase rows; [SAMPLE] rows and internal/test users excluded from production KPIs. Firebase is explicitly unavailable for current event decisioning because the Events explorer did not hydrate.</p></div></body></html>
<#/multipart>
